    "gp_section_644851814751011478": {
      "settings": {
        "checksum": "2d4d537eb274614233a11c0eb7f13691a138e36daf886939abcbd5dec329343b_1_1_1_0__1",
        "ggA9H20001_text": "<span style=\"color:#B5813A;font-size:18px;font-weight:400\">05</span> Where it won’t help",
        "ggA9Tx00001_text": "<p>It is not a simulator and it is not a coach. If you’ve never held a golf club before, take a lesson first. ARC ONE assumes you have some idea of what a swing looks like, and it works by sharpening what’s already there.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also: ten minutes a day is a <i>floor</i>, not a ceiling. The more reps you give it, the faster the click starts showing up in the right place.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The honest framing is this. A single lesson often costs more than the trainer, and the feeling fades within weeks. ARC ONE is a one-time purchase, and it gives you the same honest feedback on rep one as it does on rep ten thousand.</p>"
      },
